Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:56:39 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 36/93] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: share the keyboard backlight,
 add it to J716c

The J716c leaves fpwm0 disabled and has no keyboard backlight LED. Its
ADT has the same pwm0 kbd-backlight node as the J714s, J716s and the
K114/K116 boards: channel 0 of fpwm0 at 25 kHz.

Move the pwm-leds node and the fpwm0 enable, which the J714s and J716s
each carried as an identical copy, into a new t6050-kbd-backlight.dtsi.
Include it from the J714s, J716s, J716c and t6050-k114-k116.dtsi. The
K boards keep their own LED label and no default-state through a small
override, and keep their rear logo LED in the same controller.

The J716c gains the LED and an enabled fpwm0. The J714s, J716s, K114c,
K114s, K116c and K116s DTBs are byte-identical; no other T6050 board
changes. The J714c can take the same include.

The J714s block was added by DjDeveloperr, the J716s one by Rolando
Trevino.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
